<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korean bond market closed for Christmas day.</title>
<headline>South Korean bond market closed for Christmas day.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Korean bond market is closed on Wednesday for Christmas day. The market will reopen on Thursday.</p>
<p>Yields on benchmark three-year corporate bonds ended at 12.63 percent on Tuesday, up from the previous close at 12.58 percent.</p>
<p>--Jean Yoon (822) 727 5643</p>
